#edb/ref 1035 #uuid "340f0f9d-19b0-5cff-abb5-75d2e7e75aa9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115078 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4723" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115078 #edb/ref 1071 "The inverse of the matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115078 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7c480d6a-93a1-56ec-a75c-56402e872c92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115078 #edb/ref 1074 "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{2}R_1,\n\\qquad\nR_1 := R_1+(-3)R_2.\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](images/b3/b34f8d0d2c5f05f6c104395e75e9f5c93df7812155e09bc47828747e752d003a.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115079 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4724" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115079 #edb/ref 1071 "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine $A^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e13311fb-21de-58d4-aed0-18304b48bb0c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115079 #edb/ref 1074 "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](images/91/919674aa42fd55c536318518d9e14de07a515d3c33cb7868378ce168221f13ff.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115080 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4725" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115080 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2 \\,$ and $\\, R_2 :=  R_2+(-1)R_1?$\n\n![](images/e0/e034f65af225ce46015a5accae774a24eed8617590a583a2a885b4b1c5332103.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115080 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ff4b4389-d8ff-5b48-904b-ff405abb4e48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115080 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186383286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186398368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186398375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186401981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186401995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186573266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining the Row Operations Required To Find the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115249 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115250 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115250 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115250 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218611